	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The modeled outcome was “death or re-transplant within the indicated timeframe,” primarily at 1 year and secondarily at 3 years, so the closest allowed label is Other. Figure 1 and the Results state that all 1-year models had low AUCs ranging from 0.55 to 0.62. The paper also states that all models had NPV 0.87-0.90 and PPV <0.25, but the retrieved text does not provide model-specific numeric PPV/NPV/sensitivity/specificity values for a single chosen model, so I leave those fields NR rather than guess. Calibration was clearly reported through calibration slopes and Figures 2, 4, and 5. DCA was not reported. The LAS post-transplant survival measure had calibration slope 0.38 (95% CI 0.03-0.73), indicating overestimation of mortality risk.  ￼  ￼

